  "reason": "Evidence: The three completed experiments show a clear progression: transformer aggregation beats avgpool (+5.6 pp), and imagenet_vit_l beats resnet50 (+3.3 pp), with config_028 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat, multiprofile) achieving the best accuracy at 0.7207. The only untested variable in this top configuration is the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted). Question: Does weighted fusion improve over concat when the strong transformer+ViT-L backbone is already in place? This is a single-variable exploitation of the best-performing setup, directly testing whether the fusion mechanism can squeeze additional accuracy from the same representations. Why this is the best next experiment: With 6 experiments remaining, exploiting the strongest direction first locks in a high-accuracy baseline early. Config_039 differs from config_028 only in fusion (weighted vs. concat), so any accuracy change is cleanly attributable to fusion. Expected cost is similar to config_028 (~4.6–5.0 GPU hours) since the architecture is nearly identical—only the final fusion layer changes—making it a cheap, high-information experiment."
